        <mxCell id="AEMAzbdP2906VLopEq2b-1" parent="1" style="ellipse;shape=cloud;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="Pixel matrix;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In C or C++ it can be declared as:&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;Pixel matrix[row][column];&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In C++ a dynamic matrix can be done with std::vector:&lt;br&gt;std::vector&amp;lt;std::vector&amp;lt;Pixel&amp;gt;&amp;gt; matrix; or&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In the infocell world there is no vector, only list or maps.&lt;br&gt;Actually an infocell is already a map like datastructure, so we emulating the 2d array with&lt;br&gt;std::Map&amp;lt;keyType=Number, valueType=std::Map&amp;lt;keyType=Number, valueType=GridItem&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;std::Map here is an infocell datastructure" vertex="1">
